From: smnws <117300309+smnws@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: mediatek: model MT7981 dependencies

MT7981 has one WED engine. Permit its single phandle while preserving
the two-entry constraint on other SoCs.

The driver also requires the topmisc regmap for the USB/QPHY mux path.
Allow and require mediatek,infracfg on MT7981; omitting it prevents
Ethernet from probing before any MAC or switch interface is registered.
---
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/mediatek,net.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/mediatek,net.yaml
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@
 
   mediatek,wed:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
-    minItems: 2
+    minItems: 1
     maxItems: 2
     items:
       maxItems: 1
@@ -338,11 +338,18 @@
             - const: netsys0
             - const: netsys1
 
-        mediatek,infracfg: false
-
         mediatek,sgmiisys:
           minItems: 2
           maxItems: 2
+
+        mediatek,wed:
+          maxItems: 1
+      required:
+        - mediatek,infracfg
+    else:
+      properties:
+        mediatek,wed:
+          minItems: 2
 
   - if:
       properties:
